WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
District ideas become statewide progress.
The EEO Innovative Best Practices Grant Initiative funds district-led approaches that advance equitable hiring, retention, and institutional practice.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
$20 million for statewide EEO progress.
AB 132 established a one-time EEO Best Practices Fund. Approximately $15.5 million was apportioned to eligible districts in 2021–22.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
$5,651,806 awarded to 21 districts.
Competitive grants expanded local experimentation and created practices that other colleges can study and adapt.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:33.000
$1.4 million across 11 districts.
Awards support innovative pre-hiring, post-hiring, and EEO interventions. Five awards are $100,000 and six are $150,000.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
$7,051,806 committed through two cycles.
The competitive total is separate from the earlier statewide apportionment, preventing double counting.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Local projects. Shared learning.
Current awards are Allan Hancock Joint CCD, Antelope Valley CCD, Citrus CCD, Peralta CCD, and West Valley-Mission CCD at $100,000 each; and Kern CCD, Mt. San Antonio CCD, North Orange County CCD, San Diego CCD, Santa Monica CCD, and State Center CCD at $150,000 each.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Investment that compounds.
The initiative connects investment, implementation, learning, and shared capacity to support lasting equal employment opportunity impact.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:04.000
IBP Grant Initiative
District innovation. Shared evidence. Sustainable impact.
